      "body": "\n\n## Overview\n\nAfter `--max-model-len auto` reduces the context limit, MRV2 speculators can retain the original limit. Read the resolved limit from `ModelConfig` and cap draft attention metadata to it.\n\n## Claims\n\n- Keep draft sequence bounds within the fitted block-table capacity.\n- Preserve a smaller draft-model limit.\n\n## Validation\n\n```bash\nVLLM_TARGET_DEVICE=cpu .venv/bin/python -m pytest \\\n  tests/v1/worker/test_gpu_target_dependent_ar_speculator.py \\\n  tests/v1/spec_decode/test_eagle_draft_attn_metadata.py -q\n```\n\n28 passed. The new metadata test fails on `origin/main` (`1024 != 512`) and passes with this change.\n\n`pre-commit` and `mypy-3.12` pass on the changed files.\n\n### GPU\n\nTested with an RTX PRO 4000 Blackwell using `RedHatAI/Qwen3-8B-speculator.eagle3`.\n\n| Version | Auto-fit result | Boundary request | `bench serve` |\n|---|---:|---:|---:|\n| `origin/main` | 40960 -> 12736 | HTTP 200 | 16/16 |\n| This change | 40960 -> 12736 | HTTP 200 | 16/16 |\n\nFull GSM8K evaluation on this change:\n\n| Metric | Result |\n|---|---:|\n| Flexible extract | 0.8810 +/- 0.0089 |\n| Strict match | 0.8741 +/- 0.0091 |\n| Completed samples | 1319/1319 |\n\n<details>\n<summary>GPU commands</summary>\n\n```bash\nvllm serve RedHatAI/Qwen3-8B-speculator.eagle3 \\\n  --max-model-len auto \\\n  --gpu-memory-utilization 0.92 \\\n  --host 127.0.0.1 \\\n  --port 8000\n```\n\n```bash\nvllm bench serve \\\n  --backend openai \\\n  --base-url http://127.0.0.1:8000 \\\n  --endpoint /v1/completions \\\n  --model RedHatAI/Qwen3-8B-speculator.eagle3 \\\n  --tokenizer Qwen/Qwen3-8B \\\n  --dataset-name random \\\n  --num-prompts 16 \\\n  --random-input-len 128 \\\n  --random-output-len 32 \\\n  --request-rate inf \\\n  --seed 0\n```\n\n```bash\nlm_eval \\\n  --model local-completions \\\n  --model_args model=RedHatAI/Qwen3-8B-speculator.eagle3,base_url=http://127.0.0.1:8000/v1/completions,tokenizer=Qwen/Qwen3-8B,num_concurrent=16,tokenized_requests=False,max_length=12736 \\\n  --tasks gsm8k \\\n  --num_fewshot 5 \\\n  --batch_size 1\n```\n\n</details>\n\n## Details\n\n`DraftModelSpeculator` is created before memory profiling. It cached `max_model_len` and passed its construction-time draft limit to attention metadata after auto-fit. FlexAttention derives its logical block count from that metadata.\n\nFollowing the `ModelState` fix in #58149, the speculator now reads `max_model_len` from `ModelConfig`. The metadata limit is `min(draft_max_seq_len, max_model_len)`.\n\nNo issue or PR covers this. #58149 fixed the same stale copy in `ModelState`; #57964 covers rotary-cache sizing.\n\n---\n\n<details>\n<summary> Pull Request Checklist </summary>\n\n- [x] I used vLLM's `/pr-checklist` skill. (Mandatory for agents, optional for humans).\n- [x] AI assistance was used during the creation of this PR.\n\n- [x] **Design Fit:** Minimizes impact on core components, reuses existing functionality, and justifies added complexity.\n- [x] **Testing and Validation:** Validates the change and ensures any added tests are meaningful and reliable, with CI coverage or documented CI resource constraints and validation performed outside CI.\n- [x] **Code Quality and Style:** Keeps code and comments clear and concise, and updates relevant documentation and examples.\n- [x] **Pull Request Contents:** Includes a brief summary and relevant links, supports claims with evidence, explains root causes and implementation trade-offs, and follows the contributing guide.\n</details>\n\n",
